    <h2>About Shri Sanwaliya Seth</h2>
    <p>
        According to local belief, a milkman dreamt of idols of Lord Krishna buried in the ground near the village of
        Bhadsoda-Bagund. When the spot was dug up, three idols were found. Today they are worshipped at three temples:
        the main temple at <strong>Mandaphiya</strong>, another at <strong>Bhadsoda</strong>, and the <strong>Prakatya Sthal</strong>
        (place of appearance) where the idols were discovered.
    </p>
    <p>
        The main temple at Mandaphiya is a grand structure of carved pink stone. Its offering boxes (<em>bhandar</em>) are
        famous for the huge donations they receive &ndash; a sign of the deep faith devotees place in &ldquo;Seth&rdquo;
        Sanwaliya, who is believed to bless business and prosperity.
    </p>

    <h2>How to Reach Sanwariya Seth Temple from Chittorgarh</h2>
    <p>
        The temple lies about 40 km from Chittorgarh, a short detour off the Chittorgarh&ndash;Udaipur highway. The road is in
        good condition, and a private taxi gets you there in under an hour.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>By taxi (recommended):</strong> Door-to-door, flexible timing and the driver waits while you take darshan.</li>
        <li><strong>By bus:</strong> Buses run from Chittorgarh, but they can be crowded, especially on festival days and weekends.</li>
        <li><strong>From Udaipur:</strong> Roughly 75&ndash;80 km. We also arrange pickups from Udaipur city and the airport.</li>
    </ul>

