    <h2>Best Time to Visit</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Season:</strong> October to March is the most comfortable. Summer afternoons are very hot.</li>
        <li><strong>Time of day:</strong> Early morning is calm and ideal for darshan; weekends and holidays are busier.</li>
        <li><strong>Festivals:</strong> The Jaljhulni Ekadashi fair, Janmashtami and Holi bring huge crowds and a wonderful festive atmosphere. Book your taxi well in advance for these dates.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="callout">
        <p class="callout-title"><i class="fas fa-info-circle text-brand"></i>Temple timings</p>
        <p>
            The temple is open from early morning until late evening, with a break in the afternoon. Aarti and darshan timings
            change with the season, so check locally or ask your driver before you set out.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Combine Your Darshan With Other Places</h2>
    <p>Make the most of your trip by adding nearby places to the same day:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Chittorgarh Fort:</strong> Darshan in the morning and the fort in the afternoon makes a perfect day. See our <a href="Chittorgarh-Fort-Travel-Guide.aspx">fort guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Bhadsoda and the Prakatya Sthal:</strong> Visit all three Sanwaliya Ji temples in one trip.</li>
        <li><strong>Matri Kundiya:</strong> A sacred bathing site on the Banas river, often called the &ldquo;Haridwar of Mewar&rdquo;.</li>
        <li><strong>Nathdwara and Eklingji:</strong> Continue on to Shrinathji and Eklingji for a longer pilgrimage circuit, or go on to <a href="Chittorgarh-to-Udaipur-Taxi.aspx">Udaipur</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Tips for Devotees</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Dress modestly and keep footwear in the car or at the designated stand.</li>
        <li>Carry small change for offerings and prasad.</li>
        <li>Keep valuables to a minimum on crowded days.</li>
        <li>Senior citizens should visit early in the morning to avoid long queues.</li>
    </ul>
